# Security Rules

Scope: secret handling in this repository. See
[docs/features/secret-management.md](docs/features/secret-management.md) for the
full flow and [AGENT.md](AGENT.md) for project context.

## Never commit secret values

- No real values for `API_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL`, or any other credential in
  source, tests, docs, fixtures, or commit messages.
- `.env.example` documents variable names only; keep it value-free.
- `.env` is listed in `.gitignore` and must stay untracked. The `initialize`
  step in `environment.yaml` generates a minimal `.env` containing only
  `ENVIRONMENT`.

## Secrets come from organization blueprints

- `API_KEY` and `DATABASE_URL` are injected by Devin Cloud organization
  blueprints and re-exported in the `initialize` and `maintenance` sections of
  `environment.yaml`.
- Add new secrets at the organization level and reference them by name in
  `environment.yaml` (`export NEW_SECRET=$NEW_SECRET`); never hard-code a
  fallback value.
- Read secrets at runtime with `os.getenv(...)` only.

## Never expose secret values

- Report presence, length, and source — not the value. Follow the existing
  masking pattern in `app/main.py`:
  - `/` returns `api_key_status` as `"configured (length: N)"` or
    `"not configured"`.
  - `/secrets-status` returns `status`, `length`, and `source` per secret.
- Do not log, print, or return secret values, and do not include them in error
  messages or exception traces.
- Never echo secrets in shell commands or CI output.
